/// Sliders for a float or an integer value.
///
/// Call these inside a frame callback. Each call draws one slider and returns its `Signal`.
// Both functions are `[manual]`: SliderConfig.format is a printf template forwarded
// to a C sprintf, and whether it is valid depends on the value type (%.2f for float,
// %d for int), so the hand-written Rust binding validates it per function.
api Slider {
    /// Draws a slider for a float and returns its `Signal`.
    ///
    /// `value` is kept between `min` and `max` and is written back when the user changes it. `SliderConfig.format`
    /// sets how the value is shown beside the label, with "%.2f" as the default.
    [manual] float_impl(label: String, value: *f32, min: f32, max: f32, config: SliderConfig) -> Signal
    /// Draws a slider for an integer and returns its `Signal`.
    ///
    /// `value` is kept between `min` and `max` and is written back when the user changes it. `SliderConfig.format`
    /// sets how the value is shown beside the label, with "%d" as the default.
    [manual] int_impl(label: String, value: *i32, min: i32, max: i32, config: SliderConfig) -> Signal
}
